Falsifies `filesystem_contract::dir::Rights::a_grandchild_is_bounded_by_the_root`.

The defect: `attenuate` computes `self.0 | requested` instead of `self.0 & requested`, so a child
carries every bit it asked for and the root's mask bounds nothing. It is the same one-character
change that falsifies `attenuate_never_widens`, and that is the honest finding about this harness:
the depth-2 claim is implied by the depth-1 claim plus the associativity of `&`, so no defect
reaches one without the other. This record exists so the harness is no longer `unfalsified` while
being red under a real defect, which `attenuate_never_widens`'s own patch already said it was.

Expected to fail: `assert_eq!(grandchild.bits() & !root.bits(), 0, "a grandchild carries a bit the
root did not")`, whenever `a` or `b` holds a right the root does not.

diff --git a/crates/filesystem_contract/src/dir.rs b/crates/filesystem_contract/src/dir.rs
--- a/crates/filesystem_contract/src/dir.rs
+++ b/crates/filesystem_contract/src/dir.rs
@@ -177,7 +177,7 @@
     /// silently given less than it asked for, but that refusal is about telling the truth and
     /// this line is about the property.
     pub const fn attenuate(self, requested: u64) -> Self {
-        Rights(self.0 & requested)
+        Rights(self.0 | requested)
     }
 
